& [Delineation]
  + semantic candidate projection describes what could be built
  + build execution plan describes one exact effectful attempt
  + build capability receipt accounts requested versus admitted powers under the seed ceiling
  + sandbox admission is supplied target-host evidence and is not inferred from path strings
  + authorization certificate is Security plus external-authority permission for one plan and validity interval
  + build observation records what the runner reports occurred
  + artifact receipt identifies produced bytes but remains unverified
  + verification receipt judges exact immutable evidence but grants no signing admission installation or execution

& [CriticalReroute]
  + the candidate CandidateCompilationPlan requests semantic_read and source_read only
  + reusing its CompilerCapabilityReceipt for Build FileWrite or ProcessExecute would be capability laundering
  + Slice6 therefore owns NativeBuildExecutionPlan and NativeBuildCapabilityReceipt forms bound back to the candidate and seed ceiling
  + this is a stronger boundary than mutating or reinterpreting the Slice5 plan

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + [keys] plan_id receipt_id sandbox_admission_id approval_id authorization_id attempt_id artifact_id verification_plan_id verification_receipt_id
  + [roots] seed candidate projection toolchain build-input sandbox runner authorization artifact and verifier digests
  + [relations] candidate planned_as build_plan authorized_by approval attempted_as observation produced artifact_receipt checked_by verification_receipt
  + [states] proposed capability_accounted sandbox_admitted authorized attempted produced_unverified verification_passed verification_failed verification_unresolved
  + [constraints] exact lineage closed vocabularies finite bounds create-new paths non-overlap logical validity one artifact and domain-separated self-excluding digests

& [DualHemisphereReview]
  + [expansive] future runners may be Windows restricted token AppContainer WSL container Linux namespace VM remote builder or FPGA toolchain
  + [expansive] future artifacts may be executable library service firmware bitstream package or model-side procedure carrier
  + [convergent] P0 retains one Rust CLI one artifact one exact Cargo schema one external sandbox profile and one supplied observation
  + [convergent] runner implementation and physical containment proof remain outside cantor_core

& [SevenFoldExplosion]
  + [fold_1_identity] separates plan permission observation receipt verification and admission identities
  + [fold_2_capability] prevents read-only candidate authority from expanding into build process write network install or effect authority
  + [fold_3_physical] distinguishes lexical path safety from independently evidenced OS containment and denied roots
  + [fold_4_execution] binds argument vector environment executable cwd validity interval budgets exit and complete output accounting
  + [fold_5_artifact] distinguishes expected output from observed bytes and produced bytes from independently verified bytes
  + [fold_6_fault] preserves refusal failure timeout cancellation infrastructure fault partial artifact and stale evidence without success conversion
  + [fold_7_lifecycle] stops after verification and leaves signing admission installation deployment execution and successor recognition separately governed

& [ConstraintLedger]
  + preserve Slice5 candidate immutability and read-only projection
  + require exact native backend lineage and one artifact
  + require SourceRead Build FileWrite ProcessExecute and forbid Network Install ExternalEffect
  + require separate Security and authority signatures from seed-bound trust roots
  + require create-new disposable and output roots with repository seal credential and network denials
  + never let a successful exit imply artifact correctness or reproducibility
  + never let a passed verification imply semantic truth runtime safety permission installation or execution

& [PruningTrace]
  + pruned production ambient Command runner because no cross-platform physical sandbox denial proof is currently admitted
  + pruned shell command strings inherited environment implicit PATH and dependency fetch
  + pruned automatic signing admission installation deployment execution cleanup retry and successor replacement
  + pruned internal llama.cpp FPGA OneDrive EVO-X2 remote and Minecraft work as unrelated authority expansion

& [Uncertainty]
  + target-host physical sandbox provider and denial matrix remain unselected
  + production trust-key provisioning rotation revocation and custody remain external
  + deterministic reproducibility across operating systems toolchains timestamps linkers and file paths remains target-specific
  + behavior and interface probes beyond digest identity require later verifier programs

& [Exhaustion]
  + [gain_delta] exact later-stage capability form cryptographic dual approval supplied physical evidence and produced-versus-verified separation
  + [exhaustion_state] phase_locked_for_pure_core_forms_and_fake_runner_fixture
  + [growth_seed] separately activate a physical host runner only after admitted sandbox evidence
